# Release: v1.0.5
# Files:   dwarf_all.csv, gc_ambiguous.csv
# Fetched: 2026-07-28
#
# SatGen_Dwarf's Jdata.py read these two files over HTTPS at import time. That
# made every script network-dependent, and -- worse -- meant the dwarf sample
# could change underneath a published result if the release were re-tagged.
# The sample is not incidental: dwarf_names and five parallel arrays
# (abbreviations, fermi_names, fermi_names_update, n_stars, ps18_names) are
# positionally keyed to the order this file produces, and every `dsph_idx` CLI
# argument in the pipeline indexes it.
#
# Committed deliberately, despite being data: this is the provenance-critical
# layer, where a silent catalog swap changes every downstream number.
#
# To re-pin, bump LVDB_VERSION in python/config.py, re-fetch both files, and
# expect tests/test_dwarf_sample.py to fail until the recorded name list and
# hashes are updated -- that failure is the point.

